Wi-Fi: bounds checks for the modem's SMEM, GLINK RX and QRTR lengths (HackiOS 79b00afb70 class).

Every length below is chosen by the modem, not by us. The same audit that HackiOS made
for the redwood WLAN driver applies to SpesModem: a data padding larger than its data
wraps an SMEM item's size to about 4 GB, a GLINK OPEN/INTENT/DATA length near 4 GB wraps
to zero so rx_advance(0) never consumes the message, and hlen + size (QRTR) wraps for a
huge size. Drop malformed SMEM entries, use 64-bit message lengths, stop RX when a
message cannot fit the FIFO, and check QRTR option length and payload as subtractions.

